Windows 11 Basics Good To Know Versions ISO – Enterprise download. LTSC is a special-purpose version.

The difference:

Windows 11 Enterprise (normal)

This is what sits on most office desks in a company.
It gets a feature update every year (new features, design changes), plus the monthly security patches.
It comes with the usual extras: the Microsoft Store, the built-in apps, Widgets and so on.
It’s what you’ll be supporting on a help desk, so it’s the right match for your labs.

Windows 11 Enterprise LTSC (Long-Term Servicing Channel)

It’s frozen on one version for years. It gets security fixes only, with no new features and no surprise changes.
It’s stripped back: no Microsoft Store and most of the consumer apps removed.
It’s built for machines that must do one job reliably and never change: ATMs, factory and lab equipment, airport kiosks, and medical imaging workstations.

The reason LTSC exists for certain company's like Medical Imaging. A computer driving a scanner or running imaging software has been tested and 
certified exactly as it is, and you don’t want a yearly feature update moving things around or breaking the vendor’s software.
LTSC is Microsoft saying “this version will stay exactly as it is, just kept safe.” The normal edition is more like an everyday car that gets a full overhall every year.
